<!--Post: 4786--><!--Time: 1106750215-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4786"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 6:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK left another package in rural Sedgwick County.  A card sent to KAKE-TV led police to it.  The news article says this is package #8, and indicates there is a package #7, which has not been found. Link to article: <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10735801.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10735801.htm</a>. <BR> <BR>This begins to sound like the medallion hunt at the River Festival.  <a href="http://www.bizjournals.com/wichita/stories/2002/03/11/daily36.html" target=_top>http://www.bizjournals.com/wichita/stories/2002/03 /11/daily36.html</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4786-->
<!--Post: 4804--><!--Time: 1106757342-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;This begins to sound like the medallion hunt at the River Festival.&#34; <BR> <BR>Hey whois, <BR>It began to sound like the Medallion hunt way back in March. I&#39;ve often wondered which Eagle employees were responsible for writing the clues. It&#39;s just too strange, what with the obvious affection he has for the Eagle and KAKE TV.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4804-->
<!--Post: 4899--><!--Time: 1106799936-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4899"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Cougar and Whois: <BR> <BR>Note: The box was found on a road &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; <BR> <BR>Tom said he got a email a day before the drop from a women in a QT that saw a man open his wallet and he had a picture of Nancy Fox in it... he was asking directions if i recall Tom&#39;s message correctly. <BR> <BR>This QT is North of Ketchi... in fact it is &#34;on&#34; the North East corner of road called &#34;Ketchi&#34; I believe. <BR> <BR>A person in the chat yesterday called &#34;dreamer&#34; posted links to some maps. <BR> <BR>The first had a green line coming from the north &#40;off map&#41; south/right turn to a stop at... get this... Carol Moulds House. <BR> <BR>The road Carol Mould lived on is rt something but... becomes &#34;Ketchi&#34; something or other. <BR> <BR>I was told the names of some of these were changed such as 61st... <BR> <BR>When I asked said person &#40;dreamer&#41; why they had posted the map to Moulds Home... All I got was &#34;Who knows Q&#34; and &#34;I was just throwing it out there...trying to help&#34; <BR> <BR>Then &#34;dreamer&#34; quit chat... <BR> <BR>Hmmm... <BR> <BR>Tom told me he does not know who this is... <BR> <BR>Of course I have been in the chat before and saw some slightly sarcastic refs to Glen Campbell Lyrics &#40;actually song titles&#41; and assumed they were directed at me but would the bored and or intoxicated go this far to poke fun at me... doubt it! <BR> <BR>Really strange... especially when you keep in mind the only reason &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; came up was a apparent &#40;still not sure&#41; Map Quest snafu with the local of &#34;B&amp;K Storage&#34; at 11th &amp; Woodrow but listed as just &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; with no #s. <BR> <BR>That Dennis guy said he was in the general 11th &amp; Woodrow area &#40;my deduction by his description&#41; and got a strange feeling when he was there. <BR> <BR>Odd... Odd... Odd... <BR> <BR>Also: Post Toasties Corn Flakes in the past gave away: <BR> <BR>Train Sets <BR> <BR>Badges <BR> <BR>A Linda &#34;Williams&#34; Doll <BR> <BR>And a puppet set that has a display with cartoon children manipulating the puppets with strings that look like blind cords that go out a window &#40;see photos&#41;. <BR> <BR>Interested in your thoughts Cougar and Whois... also Analyzer if your reading this. <BR> <BR>Going to post in the &#34;North of&#34; thread as well. <BR> <BR> <BR>Here are the cereal box photo links: <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/box60.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/box60.jpg</a> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/box61.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/box61.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn28.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn28.jpg</a> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn29.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn29.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.timepassagesnostalgia.com/watermarked/images05/0553gmanad1.jpg" target=_top>http://www.timepassagesnostalgia.com/watermarked/i mages05/0553gmanad1.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/tic395.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/tic395.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Side Note: The drop site was near the: <BR>Atchison Topeka &amp; Santa Fe RR <BR> <BR>Also a song covered by many including the oft associated with &#34;Kansas&#34; Judy Garland. <BR> Interesting too... there are a lot of &#34;versions&#34; of the lyrics. <BR> <BR>Lyrics: <a href="http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=Atchison%2BTopeka%2BSanta%2BFe%2Blyrics&amp;btnG=Search" target=_top>http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=Atchison&#43; Topeka&#43;Santa&#43;Fe&#43;lyrics&amp;btnG=Search</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4899-->
<!--Post: 4911--><!--Time: 1106812548-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR> <BR>Cougar: <BR> <BR>This is really too weird.  Unless I&#39;m really drifting away from the dock, this is the only “serial” killer who sends back trophies. <BR> <BR>Now there is this macabre humor creeping into his communications.  I mean, putting this in a “cereal” box?????    <BR> <BR>A &#34;cereal&#34; killer. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4911-->
<!--Post: 4930--><!--Time: 1106829515-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4930"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stuart_m<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stuart_m<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 4:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Those kids with the puppets sure have a demented expression, do they not? Gives me the creeps more than BTK does.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4930-->
<!--Post: 4936--><!--Time: 1106832826-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4936"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 5:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;That Dennis guy said he was in the general 11th &amp; Woodrow area &#40;my deduction by his description&#41; and got a strange feeling when he was there.&#34; <BR> <BR>Really? I would like to hear more on this. That location is just a couple of short blocks from the Arthur B. Sim golf course and the Booth Home, where I believe there is some connection to this case.  <BR> <BR>And fwiw, I echo Den&#39;s &#34;feelings&#34; about this area. I always felt it too.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4936-->
<!--Post: 4939--><!--Time: 1106834882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4939"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 6:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cougar, I&#39;m glad someone else mentioned golf. Its like a park, meaning wide open with trees and the sorts. What I would like to know is how close are the murder scenes to the golf course?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4939-->
<!--Post: 4942--><!--Time: 1106835660-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4942"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 6:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Nug, <BR> <BR>Wegerle is a shout away. From the golf course you go 2 blocks north to 13th and then maybe 5 minutes or less to the west on 13th. Not sure of the mileage. Has to be a mile or less. The other confirmed scenes are east of this area, within three miles. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4942-->
<!--Post: 4953--><!--Time: 1106838752-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4953"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 7:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thx Cougar, <BR>Guess my hunch was wrong. Thought he could have found his victims fom the golf course. My bad<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4953-->
<!--Post: 5073--><!--Time: 1106863107-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5073"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 1:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Couger: <BR> <BR>You&#39;ll have to ask Dennis yourself. When he was asking people in Chat where he was by describing how he got to an area in Wichita... I threw out 11th &amp; Woodrow and Riverside and got some confirmation from others but not Dennis. <BR> <BR>He &#40;Dennis&#41; either didn&#39;t see my questions and remarks about the whole Map Quest/North of thing or he chose not to answer me. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know. <BR> <BR> <BR>I do know that for me the 401 Kansas PJs 123 ABCs thing and the North of Ketchi thing at 11th &amp; Woodrow or where the mysterious B&amp;K should be/is/isn&#39;t... has some significance... <BR> <BR>Also: Things in some very obscure way but there none the less keep coming up &#34;Pittsburgh&#34; <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know why. I know there is a &#34;Pittsburg&#34; Kansas &#40;no &#39;h&#39;&#41; but as a Steeler Fan I am tuned to Pittsburgh a bit but I didn&#39;t look for it it was there a few places that I won&#39;t go back over here. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s hard to trust anyone in this case and even on this board however Couger from talking to you I have found that I do trust you and admire your courage, as I&#39;ve said before. <BR> <BR> <BR>I have something I want to run by you but not here... I&#39;ll try and catch you on the Chat.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5073-->
<!--Post: 9677--><!--Time: 1109596575-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9677"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 5:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q-<b>WHERE</b> did you get that quote &#34;That Dennis guy said he was in the general 11th &amp; Woodrow area &#40;my deduction by his description&#41; and got a strange feeling when he was there.&#34; on Jan 26th?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9677-->
<!--Post: 9681--><!--Time: 1109597832-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9681"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 5:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The 11&amp;Woodrow came from a mapquest search &#40;see the saga of north of kechi&#41; <BR> <BR>The Pittsburg thing...that entire area kept popping up in my searches. I still think there is a whole other side to this story. Also when they were first at the courthouse friday, the reporter mentioned vans with Missouri plates pulling in &#40;in the context that it was news&#41;then I never heard another word about them. <BR> <BR>Factor X Files<!--/Text--></td></tr>
